#
# No RT group scheduling, on every board and flavor.
#
# It gives every cgroup its own RT bandwidth and throttling, and RT
# tasks in a group without bandwidth (systemd's default) can't run at
# all; its period timer also only serves its own root domain, which
# breaks with isolated CPUs (the FIXME in kernel/sched/rt.c). Not
# something to test RT latencies with. omap2plus_defconfig and
# bcm2835_defconfig (bbb, rpi3-32) turn it on, x86_64 and arm64
# defconfig don't, so the boards weren't configured alike.
#
# CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED is not set
